 { This game was played in the 2018 chess.com Speed Chess Championship finals. Up a piece for two pawns, Nakamura was winning here. However, after careful play, Carlsen managed to equalise by pushing his two queenside pawns far up the board. } 59. { -KEY- } Nf7 { The beginning of a crafty 5-move manoeuvre. The Knight was headed for d7 and the only direct way for Nakamura to stop it was to play 59...Be1 followed by Ba5 } Bh4 $4 { Nakamura overlooked Carlsen's idea } ( 59... Be1 60. Nxd6 Ba5 61. Nc8 Kb8 { The Black Bishop controls b6 and the White Knight is so near, yet so far from d7. } ) 
60. Nxd6 g4 61. Nc8+ Kb8 62. Nb6 { Black cannot stop White from playing Nd7+ followed by b8=Q. It's time to analyse it using PIE 1. Piece interaction and responsibilities: (i) White’s a6-b7 pawn duo mutually defend each other. The a6 pawn directly defends b7 while the b7 pawn threatens to Queen, preventing Kxa6. (ii) White’s Knight is the only piece on the board that can realistically control b8. (iii) White’s d5 pawn prevents Black from bringing another piece to the defense with …Nc6 or …Ne6. 2. Strategical weaknesses: (i) Black has allowed White to advance his passed pawns too far up the board. (ii) Black did not have enough defensive power. The lone King was no match for the two pawns and Knight. 3a. Changes in the position that would make this particular combination fail: (i) If the d5 pawn were removed. Black would easily play Nd4-c6 to stop the pawns. (ii) If the White King were on an unfortunate square (such as a1) that allows the Black Knight to give check while making its way to a defensive square. Had the White King been on a1, Black could play 60…Nb3+ and 61…Nc5, ready to capture on a6 with the Knight next. White would be just one move too slow in this scenario. 3b. Changes in the position that would still allow the tactic to work: (i) If the White King were on a less active square that did not allow any Knight checks, such as h1. After 61. Nc8+ Kb8, White will always have two ways to displace the Black King, c8-b6-d7 as shown in the game, and c8-e7-c6, both of which cannot be stopped. } 
