19. { -KEY- } Qxf7 $1 { This sacrifice works despite the possible zwischenzug Queen checks Black has } Qa1+ { The Queen cannot be taken immediately because of back rank issues } ( 19... Rxf7 20. Rxd8 Rf8 21. Rxf8 Ng8 22. Rxg8 { Also, the Rook cannot run away because of the classic smothered mate pattern } ) 
 ( 19... Re8 20. Qg8 Rxg8 21. Nf7 ) 
20. Kd2 { The White King now blocks his own Rook from moving to d8 } Rxf7 ( 20... Qxd1 { This move is even worse than 20...Rxf7. Black will be down a full piece. } 21. Rxd1 Rxf7 22. Nxf7 Kg8 23. Nxd8 ) 
21. Nxf7+ Kg8 22. Rxa1 Kxf7 { Smyslov resigned after a couple of moves. Let's execute PIE now. 1. Piece interaction and responsibilities: (i) White’s Queen attacked the f8 Rook and was prepared to sacrifice itself on g8 for a smothered mate. (ii) White’s h6 Knight aided the Queen in delivering the smothered mate. More importantly, it was ready to recapture on f7 with check. (iii) White’s d1 Rook was ready to deliver back rank mate on d8. 2. Strategical weaknesses: (i) Black did not defend his kingside sufficiently, in particular, the f7 square. (ii) Black had a weak back rank. (iii) d8 was unprotected. 3a. Changes in the position that would make this particular combination fail: (i) If Black’s back rank was more secure. For example, if the c8 Bishop were at b7, allowing the a8 Rook to defend d8. (ii) If f7 was sufficiently protected. For example, if Black had his a8 Rook on a7. 3b. Changes in the position that would still allow the tactic to work: (i) If White’s Knight were on e5 instead of h6. The only difference is that Black can play 19…Re8 and he is safe from a smothered mate, but White would still be winning in that variation. (ii) If White’s Knight were on g5 instead of h6. Black can, again, meet 19. Qxf7 with 19…Re8. But we have 20. Rhe1 to further add pressure to the back rank. Interestingly, the intuitive 19. Bxf6 (to remove the defender of h7) does not work. Black will play 19…Bf5 20. Bc3 Qa4 to threaten Qxc2#. White’s attack will run out of steam while Black’s pieces spring to life because White spent too much time taking the f6 Knight and then retreating. } 
