 { Black is forking the d1 Queen and the critical c2 square. Is there a way to save both? } 13. { -KEY- } Qe2 { c2 cannot be saved. Hence, White sets up a subtle counterattack. The threat is Nxf7 and this resembles the game between Alexander Alekhine and Ronald MacKay Bruce (Pattern #13). However, at first glance, White's idea does not seem promising because Black has a Bishop on g6 defending f7. } Nxc2+ 14. Kf1 ( 14. Kf2 { is good too } ) 
 ( 14. Kd2 $4 Nxa1 15. h5 Qg5 ) 
Nxa1 15. h5 { Chasing the defender of f7 away } Bb1 16. Nxf7 { And the rest is very familiar territory. } ( 16. Nxf7 Kxf7 17. Qxe6 Kf8 18. Qf7 ) 

