 { This game was played between David Navara and Melkumyan Hrant at the 2019 Gibraltar Masters. Where should the Rook run to? } 50. { -KEY- } Re5 { Black will have to trade Rooks on White's terms. Otherwise, the White Rook would get active on the 5th rank. In the game, Hrant opted to trade rooks on g6 } ( 50. Rg6 Rxg6 51. hxg6 { The problem is that the g6 and g7 pawn blockade ensures that Black will get a draw. As soon as White converts his Queenside majority to a single passed pawn, Black will give the Bishop up for the pawn and scoot the King over to the h8 corner, if not f8. That endgame resembles the Giri – Shankland game (Pattern #16). } ) 

