 { This is an old game played back in 1929 between Fred Dewhirst Yates (White) and Frank Marshall (Black) . Yates was easily winning until his last move, Kc3. How can Black save himself? } 1... { -KEY- } b1=Q 2. Qxb1+ Kxb1 3. Kb4 Kb2 { Similar to the Lasker - Tarrasch game (Pattern #17), Black gains this free move by threatening to Queen his a-pawn } ( 3... Kc2 $4 4. f4 a3 5. Kxa3 ) 
